# ── MARK LIII — what never belongs in the repository ──────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.
#
# NOTE: gitignore has no inline-comment syntax. A '#' that is not at the start
# of a line is part of the pattern, and a trailing '/' matches directories only.
# So every pattern below sits on its own line, with its explanation above it —
# a pattern like `config/api_keys.json  # api key` silently matches nothing.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────

# Your Gemini API key, plus per-plugin credentials (email password, app secrets).
config/api_keys.json
# Editor/backup copies that shadow the live config.
config/api_keys.json.*

# The dashboard's TLS private key and certificate.
config/certs/

# A LINKED WhatsApp session — committing it hands somebody your WhatsApp
# account, not just a key.
config/whatsapp_web/

# Google OAuth tokens (Gmail / Calendar plugins) and client secrets.
# The leading '*' matters: the file is normally `google_token.json` (or
# `oauth_token.json`), not `token.json`, so `**/token*.json` alone missed it.
**/*token*.json
**/client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json
.env
.env.*

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
memory/long_term.json
memory/*.db
memory/notes/
memory/notes_index.json
memory/calendar.json

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
# The Windows "> nul" redirect creates a real file named "nul" on POSIX shells.
nul

# ── Runtime output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
downloads/
screenshots/
uploads/
